## Problem Analysis

The snitch moves along a polyline at constant speed vs. Harry can move at speed vp in any direction. Harry catches the snitch when they're at the same position at the same time.

For each segment of the polyline:
1. The snitch arrives at vertex Vi at time cum_time[i]
2. The snitch leaves for Vi+1 at speed vs
3. Harry needs to reach the snitch's position at time t at distance dist(vp*t) from HP's start
4. Binary search to find the earliest valid meeting time

